  "final": "All verifications pass. Summary of the change:\n\n**src/repository.py**\n- `find(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` now filters on `id=? AND tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`, all bound as parameters.\n- `listing(connection, tenant, owner)` now filters on `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`, ordered by `id`, all bound as parameters.\n- `decode`/result shape unchanged: only `id`, `title`, `body` — no deletion metadata leaks.\n\n**src/service.py**\n- `get_document` and `list_documents` now pass `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository instead of ignoring `tenant` and dropping `tenant` from the listing call.\n\n**Verification**\n- `python3 checks/public.py` passes.\n- Edge cases confirmed: cross-tenant, cross-owner, deleted, and missing IDs all return `None` indistinguishably; lists are ordered by `id` and exclude deleted/other-tenant/other-owner rows; tenant/owner values containing single quotes (`t'x`, `o'w`) match correctly because queries use bound parameters, and injection-style strings like `o' OR '1'='1` are treated as literal values.",
